      "widgets_values": [
        "TILE DETAILER (MPI-1038) - Fabio's bench recipe as a Flow.\n\n1. Input_Upscale_Factor: lanczos upscale BEFORE the detail pass. 1.0 = detail only (PIL returns a same-size resize untouched).\n2. ImpactMakeTileSEGS cuts the picture into 1024 tiles with 200 px overlap and irregular masks (no tile grid), each sampled with 1.5x context.\n3. Klein 9B redraws every tile at Input_Denoise (0.35: adds detail, keeps content and palette; 0.45 already changes too much). guide_size 1024 / max_size 1536: a tile under 1024 (a small picture, detail only) is sampled at ~1 MP and scaled back, because denoise is relative to the working size - at its own 0.4 MP a photo's benches and paving were redrawn (MPI-1038).\n\nInput_Positive is sampled on EVERY tile: describe the look ('2D flat shader, cartoon'), never the scene, or flat sky tiles grow houses (MPI-623 sky ghosting).\n\nNot a 360 graph: the tiles do not wrap, so a pano's seam re-opens (MPI-623 wrap pad)."
      ],
      "title": "Tile Detailer - read me",
      "color": "#332922",
      "bgcolor": "#593930"
    }
